# Cross-platform checkout rules. Added 2026-09-04 alongside the fix for a repo
# that could not be cloned on Windows at all (see
# home/.chezmoiscripts/run_onchange_after_30-user-units.sh.tmpl for that one).
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS EVEN THOUGH EVERY TARGET IS LINUX. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. Nothing
# here is ever RUN on Windows - but the files get committed back from there,
# and a shell script that picks up CRLF fails on Linux in the least helpful way
# possible:
#     ./bootstrap.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
# A `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang fails with "no such file or directory"
# naming a binary that plainly exists. Config files are just as bad and quieter:
# systemd, sysctl and fontconfig will happily parse a trailing \r into a value.
#
# So: normalise everything to LF in the index and check it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touched, never diffed as text. Without these, `git
# diff` on the 3840x2160 wallpaper tries to print 4 MB of PNG.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Linguist: this is a dotfiles repo, so report it as Shell rather than letting
# the vendored zsh syntax-highlighting theme and the JSON configs decide.
*.tsv       linguist-language=TSV
docs/*.md   linguist-documentation
